{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02207",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.05,
      "end_seconds": 4.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Sorry, doctor, shall I sit here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.79,
      "end_seconds": 10.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "Yes, have a seat. Tell me what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.39,
      "end_seconds": 17.84,
      "duration_seconds": 5.45,
      "text": "Mm, so the thing is, I've got being very breathless."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.9,
      "end_seconds": 23.91,
      "duration_seconds": 5.01,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.71,
      "end_seconds": 53.42,
      "duration_seconds": 25.71,
      "text": "Yes, lying flat. That makes it worse. It happens a couple of times a week. Sitting up helps a bit. I'd give it a six, out of ten. I've also had a pounding heart. And, And I've been sweating as well. Uh, about sweating, pretty mild, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.72,
      "end_seconds": 60.68,
      "duration_seconds": 6.96,
      "text": "Understood. Have you had being very breathless before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.03,
      "end_seconds": 66.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "I had a similar thing last winter. It went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.24,
      "end_seconds": 83.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "What operations have you had, if any?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.21,
      "end_seconds": 91.57,
      "duration_seconds": 7.36,
      "text": "Let me think, yes, I had part of my thyroid removed, years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.83,
      "end_seconds": 101.59,
      "duration_seconds": 5.76,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.58,
      "end_seconds": 119.94,
      "duration_seconds": 14.36,
      "text": "I smoke roughly a pack every two days. I swim twice a week. I look after my grandchildren most days. My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.69,
      "end_seconds": 126.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.72,
      "text": "So, has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.51,
      "end_seconds": 131.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Right, no allergies at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.51,
      "end_seconds": 136.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.96,
      "end_seconds": 147.19,
      "duration_seconds": 9.23,
      "text": "I take something called telm... telmisartan, 40 milligrams, maybe, once a day for my pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.94,
      "end_seconds": 152.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "Have you got the box or the prescription on you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.77,
      "end_seconds": 160.38,
      "duration_seconds": 6.61,
      "text": "So, uh, no, it's at home. Losartan I don't take anymore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.91,
      "end_seconds": 165.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.04,
      "end_seconds": 177.34,
      "duration_seconds": 7.3,
      "text": "Yes, high blood pressure. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.29,
      "end_seconds": 186.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "Mm, okay. Have you had any wheeze or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.14,
      "end_seconds": 191.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "No, I'd have said so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.12,
      "end_seconds": 193.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "Any calf pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.05,
      "end_seconds": 198.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Not that I've noticed, no calf pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.18,
      "end_seconds": 202.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 203.65,
      "end_seconds": 206.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Bowels are regular, nothing odd."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.95,
      "end_seconds": 210.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Any muscle or joint problems besides this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 211.33,
      "end_seconds": 213.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.54,
      "end_seconds": 224.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Let me get the readings out of the way."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.3,
      "end_seconds": 234.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.54,
      "end_seconds": 263.13,
      "duration_seconds": 15.59,
      "text": "Okay: oxygen saturation is 94 percent, pulse is 91 beats a minute. And BP is 119 over 80, BMI works out to 26.3, height 184 centimetres, temperature is 36.9 degrees, weight 89 kilos."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.34,
      "end_seconds": 268.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "Could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.61,
      "end_seconds": 272.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "Let me feel here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.78,
      "end_seconds": 288.08,
      "duration_seconds": 6.3,
      "text": "There are crackles all the way up both lungs and you are breathing very fast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.32,
      "end_seconds": 296.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.55,
      "end_seconds": 321.32,
      "duration_seconds": 13.77,
      "text": "Putting it all together, my working impression is acute pulmonary oedema. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. Another possibility is a severe chest infection."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 322.85,
      "end_seconds": 325.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.27,
      "end_seconds": 338.32,
      "duration_seconds": 11.05,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with acute pulmonary oedema do well once it's treated properly. Let's get an ECG, for pulmonary oedema."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 340.11,
      "end_seconds": 342.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "The earliest is Tuesday, 10 am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 343.45,
      "end_seconds": 346.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "Tuesday, that works for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.58,
      "end_seconds": 380.53,
      "duration_seconds": 32.95,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange blood tests for pulmonary oedema. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. We should do a chest X-ray for pulmonary oedema. I'll start you on furosemide, 40 milligrams, once now, single dose. That's for fluid on the lungs. Sit upright, I am giving oxygen and a water tablet injection now. Let's get you seen by the emergency team, I'll arrange the letter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 382.23,
      "end_seconds": 398.02,
      "duration_seconds": 15.79,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 399.84,
      "end_seconds": 404.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "Well, um, okay, I'll look out for that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 405.7,
      "end_seconds": 412.6,
      "duration_seconds": 6.9,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again straight away. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 413.37,
      "end_seconds": 419.77,
      "duration_seconds": 6.4,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, no, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    }
  ]
}